      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T16:04:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, previously they implicitly defaulted to `CONFIG_CROS_EC_RO\u003dy` because `config CROS_EC_RO` was the first entry listed under the `choice` prompt in `zephyr/app/ec/Kconfig` (which lacked an explicit `default`).\n\nHowever, fingerprint code is strictly RW-only (`common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc` raises `#error \"fpsensor code should not be in RO image.\"` under `CONFIG_CROS_EC_RO`). Adding `default CROS_EC_RW` in `zephyr/app/ec/Kconfig` shifts these single-image unit tests to default to `CROS_EC_RW\u003dy`.\n\nSince RW builds default `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ROLLBACK_UPDATE` to `n`, I also enabled `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ROLLBACK_UPDATE\u003dy` in `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/prj.conf` so `rollback_add_entropy()` remains available test.",
